{"title":"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Are there any triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/721be88b352c335671c8de6ee706901dc48fd7b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-2)(b-2)(c-2) + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"18\" /> is prime that properly divides the positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/4114aba4b0af237582e5a0a360ce6c27ae18de4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + abc - 2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"198\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a858574aef39ba200256cf9e88687a010f78e922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{no}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11bbda318e782a50375be00dc65388f9fa08711d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z) = (a-2, b-2, c-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/0495f82cb98c70f262b2693e22d5d8773e1815d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mathbb{Z}^+ \\ni \\frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + abc - 2017}{(a-2)(b-2)(c-2)+12} = \\frac{(x-2)^2 + (y-2)^2 + (z-2)^2 + (x-2)(y-2)(z-2) - 2017}{xyz+12}\\]\" width=\"756\" height=\"44\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8366cb31efbbcb5c71d152a928a582dc05d159c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{(x+y+z-41)(x+y+z+49)}{xyz+12}+1\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"42\" /> It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f745501f99039ecaffe35b42f3fed541d98dea30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z&gt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255aee7c129ddfaf9454b17ab1305975451dadb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> is prime, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb243e0462be5d0846299dd936b63fc01ff25f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xyz+12 \\mid x+y+z-41 \\quad (1) \\quad \\text{ or } xyz+12\\mid x+y+z+49\\quad (2)\\]\" width=\"517\" height=\"18\" />\nNow, we do casework based on the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> 's in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 1: No <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> 's.</b> \n</p><p>Then, note that two of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/4/f745501f99039ecaffe35b42f3fed541d98dea30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z&gt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca995dc244ccd8fb8b7d865025e6c09597488c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz\\geq 2(x+y+z) &gt; x+y+z+37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"290\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/0103803dd177fa8ed3994987678a466e67f7b180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z) = (t, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> can't be true. Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0d6b507b72cad34192dff0157bfc86b4077fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+12\\mid 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />.  But, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968e1f3cc1d1ceafbfcba4ab0522b6348b6aafdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+2&gt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, a contradiction. \n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 2: 2 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> 's</b> \n</p><p>Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0147320c93bd47fe32bfb780514a1c98062dc8ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)=(t, -1, -1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />. Again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> can't be true, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f1ce7d1137ef96f1c3220da58dfb605a8ec8ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+12\\mid t+47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />. But, as with before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968e1f3cc1d1ceafbfcba4ab0522b6348b6aafdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t+2&gt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />\n, a contradiction.\n</p><p>-sillybone\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is no. Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb85168413e7c530f62acf892b21b90a6032aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a-2,y=b-2,z=c-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e33deeab699b4d6cc2e921ac977c29d68fce17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z\\geq -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/51045d55c252ea74952a518a99f1fb805ec4bc61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2+c^2+abc-2017=(x+y+z-41)(x+y+z+49)+xyz+12.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"20\" /> It is given in the problem that this is positive. Now, suppose for the sake of contradiction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255aee7c129ddfaf9454b17ab1305975451dadb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> is a prime. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705ed53e879f0c4fb31c1e542e694d0ab6e5bb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804ca1b88906722bd11326722238bb07b6b19ef3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(x+y+z-41)(x+y+z+49)}{xyz+12}\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"42\" /> is an integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This also implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f8447bef73b0d058a9389a184f51a4a81d29bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z &gt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255aee7c129ddfaf9454b17ab1305975451dadb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> is prime, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b6f0ecfc36f0dfefd913b8e3a4997f2ef3b1c45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xyz+12\\mid x+y+z-41\\text{ or } xyz+12\\mid x+y+z+49.\\]\" width=\"426\" height=\"18\" /> Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> must be odd, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/255aee7c129ddfaf9454b17ab1305975451dadb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" /> is odd while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f71234f8e1235efdec5531fcd2119f64294816d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z-41,x+y+z+49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"17\" /> are even. So, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f936bdb0a5f1c642fccb166d1aade2f4ea6bf3be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xyz+12\\mid x+y+z-41\\text{ or }xyz+12\\mid x+y+z+49,\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"18\" /> we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d143a1f0e435a78ccd505c6ea45aa9afc91869d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(xyz+12)\\leq x+y+z-41\\text{ or }2(xyz+12)\\leq x+y+z+49.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"18\" /> Now suppose WLOG that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c2e8c17cff668023b2f29f2e95e4a0fafa6271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d6288d0a3b3afcd57198a6c5cf923ebe29b97078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />. Then we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19db4189b37f73298ac5313edda8fd7c1e5900f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz\\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />, impossible since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c873dbfa27c1343de420037be8a1839488cf3220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z&gt;41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />. Again, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c3a8c304e15c704be1d4cabe0f6591334fe6af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Then we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad83f6d5fd632e8dd3fe7a4cb9dd129384331730.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(z+12)\\leq z-43\\text{ or }2(z+12)\\leq z+47,\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"18\" /> and since in this case we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0740acac8f3bf4ab6a4e51d8183b63a7cd8457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, this is also impossible.\nThen the final case is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> are positive odd numbers. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e123bd28da0fbd7453da503e27da65d53c1dc96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz&gt;x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34edac72137d5edb01630bd1f0254a6e2c1e6324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc&gt;a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c58c1b5fa66054afe4c94a90b45d38245c12679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;x,b&gt;y,c&gt;z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />. Then we only need to prove the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c890e767116f0d850dd5e1f0be18f91a86be4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786294ba81c75be655bda0e12c983b0ef8919a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> is odd. Then one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65ef4d0708264b7c1d1d884ba2471860f670731.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(xyz+12)\\leq 2\\text{ and/or }2(xyz+12)\\leq 92\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"18\" /> is true, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f663dc4da5c252b43fd73d042fba721a864687d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz\\leq -11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85d72c705e3658425e19e401105ee4ca6dd2394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz\\leq 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />. But if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c890e767116f0d850dd5e1f0be18f91a86be4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaaddb04c6415fe277f611552546e4da233fa495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1,y=1,z=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"17\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109ec403a99190fa3cd2161801db2e691145a42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz\\geq 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />. This is a contradiction, so we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO\" title=\"2017 USAJMO\">2017 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004121\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 359/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 991/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11845/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.861      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n100.00%   11.861      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15567:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018004121 and revision id 288465. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}